{ Your knight sits on f2, forking his queen and the pawn on h3. }
9. Bxf7+ { His bishop takes f7 with check, his toughest try. Your king must move. Where? } 9... Kf8 { Right: the king steps aside. Taking the bishop would let his rook take your knight with check. [%csl Gf8] } (9... Kd8 { Also good: d8 works too, but on f8 the king keeps the bishop under attack. } 10. Qh5 Nxe4+ 11. d4 Bxd4+ 12. Kh2 { Much better for you, but the win is longer from d8. [%csl Gd4] }) (9... Ke7 { Also winning, but the king stands in the way of your pieces. } 10. Qh5 Nxe4+ 11. d4 Bxd4+ 12. Kh2 { Much better for you, with your king a little more exposed. [%csl Be7] }) (9... Kxf7 { Taking the bishop walks into it: his pieces hit your knight on f2. } 10. d4 Rf8 11. Be3 Kg8 12. Bxf2 { Better for him: your knight is gone, and your attack with it. [%csl Rf2] }) 10. Qh5 { His queen offers a trade of queens, his best try. The knight check on h3 was the answer last time. Is it now? } 10... Nxe4+ { Right: the knight takes his pawn and uncovers your bishop: check to his king on g1! [%cal Gc5g1] } (10... Nxh3+ { The same knight check as before, but here his king steps to h2 and his queen covers. } 11. Kh2 Bd6+ 12. e5 Bxe5+ 13. Qxe5 { Much better for him: his queen took your bishop, and your attack has run out. [%csl Re5] }) (10... Qxh5 { Trading queens lets his bishop take back, and his king is safe. } 11. Bxh5 g6 12. Be2 { Much better for him: your knight on f2 is trapped, and his rook and king both hit it. [%csl Rf2] }) (10... Nd3+ { A check that only draws: his king runs, and you have nothing more. } 11. Kh2 Bd6+ 12. Kg1 { Level: the checks give you a draw at best, and the winning move was missed. [%csl Rd3] }) (10... Bxh3 { The bishop grabs a pawn, but his queen takes yours. } 11. Qxh4 { Lost for you: his queen took yours on h4. [%csl Rh4] }) 11. Qxc5+ { His queen takes your bishop with check, his best: anything else loses faster. Take her. } 11... Nxc5 { Your knight takes his queen. You gave a bishop, he gave his queen: much better for you. [%csl Gc5] } 0-1


